From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tom Englund <tomenglund26@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 14:35:29 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] nvkms: keep nvidia-drm's in-fence display semaphores in
 system memory

For every plane with an in-fence, nv_drm_atomic_commit() picks a display
semaphore with nvKms->tryInitDisplaySemaphore(), which reads the
semaphore's current value from the CPU to check that the display engine
has released it. On dGPUs the KAPI semaphore pool is allocated in video
memory, so that check is an uncached read through BAR1.

On an RTX 4080 Laptop (AD104) playing an NVDEC video stream in Firefox
under KWin (240 Hz eDP), that single read cost 125-150 us on every fenced
commit: LBR branch stacks show exactly one try per commit (no scan over
busy slots), and function_graph shows commits with an in-fence at p50
169 us against 36 us for commits without one. That is about 3 % of a
240 Hz frame, spent on the compositor's commit thread.

Allocate the pool in system memory instead, the way the KAPI notifier
surface already is. The allocation uses the display NISO coherency mode
(write-back if display NISO access is coherent, otherwise write-combined),
so the display engine sees the CPU's READY writes and the CPU sees the
engine's DONE releases, as it does for notifiers. SOC display keeps using
system memory as before.

The choice is made when nvidia-drm sets up the device. The new
nvidia_modeset.kapi_sysmem_semaphores parameter (default Y, 0444) can be
set to N on the kernel command line or in modprobe.d to return to video
memory.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 kernel-open/nvidia-modeset/nvidia-modeset-linux.c   | 12 ++++++++++++
 .../nvidia-modeset/nvidia-modeset-os-interface.h    |  1 +
 src/nvidia-modeset/kapi/src/nvkms-kapi.c            | 13 +++++++++++--
 .../include/nvidia-modeset-os-interface.h           |  1 +
 4 files changed, 25 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/kernel-open/nvidia-modeset/nvidia-modeset-linux.c b/kernel-open/nvidia-modeset/nvidia-modeset-linux.c
index 6608c919..b65f927e 100644
--- a/kernel-open/nvidia-modeset/nvidia-modeset-linux.c
+++ b/kernel-open/nvidia-modeset/nvidia-modeset-linux.c
@@ -167,6 +167,13 @@ MODULE_PARM_DESC(dp_sst_edid_recovery_fix,
 static bool dp_sst_edid_recovery_fix = true;
 module_param_named(dp_sst_edid_recovery_fix, dp_sst_edid_recovery_fix, bool, 0444);
 
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(kapi_sysmem_semaphores,
+                 "Keep the nvidia-drm display semaphores (used for plane in-fences) in system memory "
+                 "instead of video memory, so the CPU check on every fenced commit doesn't read video "
+                 "memory over PCIe. Read when the GPU is set up for nvidia-drm.");
+static bool kapi_sysmem_semaphores = true;
+module_param_named(kapi_sysmem_semaphores, kapi_sysmem_semaphores, bool, 0444);
+
 /* Fail allocating the RM core channel for NVKMS using the i-th method (see
  * FailAllocCoreChannelMethod). Failures not using the i-th method are ignored. */
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(fail_alloc_core_channel, "Control testing for hardware core channel allocation failure");
@@ -263,6 +270,11 @@ NvBool nvkms_dp_sst_edid_recovery_fix(void)
     return dp_sst_edid_recovery_fix;
 }
 
+NvBool nvkms_kapi_sysmem_semaphores(void)
+{
+    return kapi_sysmem_semaphores;
+}
+
 NvBool nvkms_conceal_vrr_caps(void)
 {
     return conceal_vrr_caps;
diff --git a/kernel-open/nvidia-modeset/nvidia-modeset-os-interface.h b/kernel-open/nvidia-modeset/nvidia-modeset-os-interface.h
index 78a79804..3103e42e 100644
--- a/kernel-open/nvidia-modeset/nvidia-modeset-os-interface.h
+++ b/kernel-open/nvidia-modeset/nvidia-modeset-os-interface.h
@@ -134,6 +134,7 @@ enum NvKmsDebugForceColorSpace nvkms_debug_force_color_space(void);
 NvBool nvkms_enable_overlay_layers(void);
 NvBool nvkms_debug_logging(void);
 NvBool nvkms_dp_sst_edid_recovery_fix(void);
+NvBool nvkms_kapi_sysmem_semaphores(void);
 void nvkms_extcon_report_hdmi(NvBool state);
 void nvkms_extcon_report_hdmi_audio(NvBool state);
 
diff --git a/src/nvidia-modeset/kapi/src/nvkms-kapi.c b/src/nvidia-modeset/kapi/src/nvkms-kapi.c
index d8b8d468..ac55a303 100644
--- a/src/nvidia-modeset/kapi/src/nvkms-kapi.c
+++ b/src/nvidia-modeset/kapi/src/nvkms-kapi.c
@@ -665,8 +665,17 @@ static NvBool KmsAllocateDevice(struct NvKmsKapiDevice *device)
         goto done;
     }
 
-    /* Allocate semaphore memory in video memory whenever available */
-    if (!nvKmsKapiAllocateSemaphores(device, !device->isSOC)) {
+    /*
+     * Allocate semaphore memory in video memory whenever available, unless
+     * nvkms_kapi_sysmem_semaphores() asks for system memory: nvidia-drm reads
+     * a semaphore from the CPU on every commit with a plane in-fence, and an
+     * uncached read of video memory through BAR1 took ~130 us on a dGPU
+     * (AD104). The display engine already accesses the notifier surface in
+     * system memory the same way.
+     */
+    if (!nvKmsKapiAllocateSemaphores(device,
+                                     !device->isSOC &&
+                                     !nvkms_kapi_sysmem_semaphores())) {
         nvKmsKapiLogDebug(
             "Failed to allocate Semaphore objects for GPU ID 0x%08x",
             device->gpuId);
diff --git a/src/nvidia-modeset/os-interface/include/nvidia-modeset-os-interface.h b/src/nvidia-modeset/os-interface/include/nvidia-modeset-os-interface.h
index 78a79804..3103e42e 100644
--- a/src/nvidia-modeset/os-interface/include/nvidia-modeset-os-interface.h
+++ b/src/nvidia-modeset/os-interface/include/nvidia-modeset-os-interface.h
@@ -134,6 +134,7 @@ enum NvKmsDebugForceColorSpace nvkms_debug_force_color_space(void);
 NvBool nvkms_enable_overlay_layers(void);
 NvBool nvkms_debug_logging(void);
 NvBool nvkms_dp_sst_edid_recovery_fix(void);
+NvBool nvkms_kapi_sysmem_semaphores(void);
 void nvkms_extcon_report_hdmi(NvBool state);
 void nvkms_extcon_report_hdmi_audio(NvBool state);
 
